UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|A short comment on the bidding. Personally, I very much dislike bidding 3 of a minor after opening 2@C. Although that is a possible bid, I would have bid 2N with the East hand. Further, after 2N it is fine to play regular |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=stayman,Stayman^*N|CP||FP||at| here. But I prefer playing what is known as |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=puppetstayman,Puppet Stayman^*N|CP||FP||at| over 2N openers and 2N rebids after 2@C. |
PG| ***** 17 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The advantage of |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=puppetstayman,Puppet Stayman^*N|CP||FP||at| is you can find out if opener has both a 5-card major or a 4-card major and differentiate between the two. On this particular hand it doesn't matter so we did go with regular |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=stayman,Stayman^*N|CP||FP||at|.|
PG| ***** 18 ***** |


