mb|P|mb|P|mb|1C|mb|1D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|1@D is fine and a standard bid. But given partner (South) is a passed hand, I would have bid 2@D with the North hand.|
PG| ***** 20 ***** |


mb|1H|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Note that if North bid 2@D, that would make it much harder for East to bid which is why you should strain to preempt when appropriate.|
PG| ***** 21 ***** |


mb|P|mb|1S|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|2C|mb|P|mb|2H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Note that West showed 3 card heart support on this auction and at least 4 clubs and possibly even 5 clubs because the only way West can have 3 clubs is if she started with 4-4 in the majors. |
PG| ***** 22 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|But if that were the case, West would have raised 1@H to 2@H. The auction by West shows specifically 4 spades and 3 hearts. And further, indicates the hand either has 4 clubs and 2 diamonds or 5 clubs and 1 diamond. Moreover, now East knows they are playing in a 7-card fit.|
PG| ***** 23 ***** |


